      "quote": "A.7.6\nPERFORMANCE ON DIFFERENT ANSWER NUMBERS\nWe also present the performance of RoG and its variants on questions with different numbers of\nanswers in Table 18. From results, we can see that RoG achieves better performance than its variants\non questions with different numbers of answers. Specifically, with the number of answer increasing,\nthe performance of RoG w/o planning decreases significantly due to the lack of knowledge from\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\nTop-K relation paths\n0\n10\n20\n30\n40\n# Retrieved Reasoning Paths\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\nTop-K relation paths\n0\n25\n50\n75\n100\n125\n# Retrieved Reasoning Paths\n0.5\n1.0\n1.5\nRetrieval Time (s)\n1e−3\nWebQSP\n1.0\n1.5\n2.0\n2.5\nRetrieval Time (s)\n1e−3\nCWQ\n# Retrieved Reasoning Paths\nRetrieval Time\nFigure 4: Average retrieval time and average number of retrieved reasoning paths w.r.t. the number\nof top-K relation paths.\n21\n\nPublished as a conference paper at ICLR 2024\nTable 17: F1 scores of RoG and its variants for different hops of questions.\nMethods\nWebQSP\nCWQ\n1 hop\n2 hop\n≥3 hop\n1 hop\n2 hop\n≥3 hop\nRoG\n77.03\n64.86\n-\n62.88\n58.46\n37.82\nRoG w/o reasoning\n57.06\n25.49\n-\n17.06\n34.25\n17.07\nRoG w/o planning\n50.33\n51.66\n-\n31.04\n33.93\n23.29\nTable 18: F1 scores of RoG and its variants for questions with varying numbers of answers.\nMethods\nWebQSP\nCWQ\n#Ans = 1\n2 ≥#Ans ≤4\n5 ≥#Ans ≤9\n#Ans ≥10\n#Ans = 1\n2 ≥#Ans ≤4\n5 ≥#Ans ≤9\n#Ans ≥10\n",
